3:## Build and checks
15:`make build` compiles the Rust binaries and builds `cli/dist` (`npm --prefix cli run build`). `make test` runs the Rust and TypeScript suites and the repository security gates. The Cloudflare service has separate setup and tests; see [the contest entry](CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md).
17:## Release package
30:Packaging builds the Rust binaries inside the approved, digest-pinned builder image (`APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE` in the `Makefile`) by default. Unless `NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1` is set, `scripts/package-linux.sh` exits with status 2 if `NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE` is unset; it always exits with status 2 if the variable names any other image. The release-tools install and license-notice generation also use an immutable, digest-pinned Node 24 image by default and require Docker, even when host Rust builds are enabled. For local packaging without Docker, set `NEXUS_RELEASE_TOOLS_NODE24_BIN` to a trusted Node 24.22.2 `bin` directory containing `node` and `npm` 11.19.1; the script checks both versions and uses that directory only for the release-tools install and notice command. The CLI install/build stays on the existing `PATH` (Node 22.22.1/npm 10.9.4 in release workflows). To package without Docker locally, also set `NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1` and leave `NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE` unset. `make verify-reproducibility` uses the pinned Docker builder and compares the archive, `SHA256SUMS`, notices, SBOM and `install.sh` byte for byte. Host-built packages are not release candidates.
